    <summary>Beta of CodeShellManager 2: a multi-terminal host for Claude Code and other CLI coding agents, driven from its UI, the csm CLI or over MCP.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
**CodeShellManager 2 (beta)** is the cross-platform rewrite of CodeShellManager in Rust: a desktop app for running many AI coding agents side by side (Claude Code, Codex, Copilot or any CLI tool). It installs beside CodeShellManager 1.x (the `codeshellmanager` package) and does not replace it.

## Features

* Many live sessions in Focus, Side by side, Overview, Grid and Free layouts; floating and torn-off panes
* A Needs-you inbox, command palette (Ctrl+K) and quick-open (Ctrl+T)
* Local, SSH and WSL sessions; sleep, wake and restore
* Full-text search over session output, notes per folder, run commands, git status and worktrees
* The `csm` CLI and an MCP server (`csm mcp`) so agents can drive it
* Tray icon and Windows notifications

## Requirements

* Windows 10 (1903+) or Windows 11, x64. No WebView2 needed.

## License

Open source under the [MIT License](https://github.com/umage-ai/CodeShellManager/blob/main/LICENSE).
]]></description>
